// The directory's screen. It shows the drive in use; each picture's line, P1 to P8 down the
// left and P9 to P16 down the right, its label and its name, taking the pen so that the
// picker's taps find them; and the key, OK or Cancel, where the keyboard's OK is; then its
// halt. tpGetDir writes the drive's digit and the sixteen names, kbOpen the key's text and its
// parameter word, before frameGo points here. It holds no jump or save, as the keyboard's list
